description:
Small change to not report `getValue()` until after the prismEditor is ready.

<details><summary>Example app</summary>

In this example, prior to the change, initializing the code editor would cycle through `""` and the value of the code once set up.

```r
library(shiny)
pkgload::load_all()
library(bslib)

ui <- page_sidebar(
  title = "Code Editor Visibility Toggle",
  sidebar = sidebar(
    actionButton("toggle", "Toggle Code Editor", class = "btn-primary"),
    hr(),
    p("Click the button to show/hide the code editor."),
    p("When visible, type in the editor to see toast notifications.")
  ),
  card(
    card_header("Code Editor Area"),
    uiOutput("code_editor_ui")
  )
)

server <- function(input, output, session) {
  # Reactive to track visibility state
  visible <- reactiveVal(TRUE)

  # Toggle visibility when button is clicked
  observeEvent(input$toggle, {
    visible(!visible())
  })

  # Render UI to control visibility while keeping input stable
  output$code_editor_ui <- renderUI({
    # Create a div that always contains the code editor
    # but use CSS to control visibility
    req(visible())

    input_code_editor(
      "code",
      label = "Enter your code:",
      value = isolate(input$code) %||%
        "# Write your R code here\nprint('Hello, World!')",
      height = "300px",
      language = "r"
    )
  })

  # Track previous value to detect changes
  previous_value <- reactiveVal(NULL)

  # Observe code editor changes and emit toasts
  observeEvent(input$code, {
    current_value <- input$code
    prev <- previous_value()

    # Only show toast if we have a previous value (skip initial load)
    if (!is.null(prev)) {
      if (current_value == "" || is.null(current_value)) {
        show_toast(toast(
          "Cleared input editor",
          icon = icon("trash")
        ))
      } else if (is.null(prev)) {
        show_toast(toast(
          "First update to editor input",
          icon = icon("code")
        ))
      } else if (!identical(current_value, prev)) {
        show_toast(toast(
          "Editor input changed",
          icon = icon("code")
        ))
      }
    }

    # Update previous value
    previous_value(current_value)
  })
}

shinyApp(ui, server)

```

</details>

Could bslib provide modern aliases for Shiny UI functions? This PR aims to answer that question by starting with aliases for Shiny functions that have also been ported to Shiny for Python, using naming conventions that are familiar to tidyverse users and consistent with the Shiny for Python API (these are generall well-aligned).

In addition to helping to nudge naming conventions away from camel case, this PR will also help give bslib some flexibility in providing its own implementations of these inputs. This will make it easier for bslib to eventually provide inputs tailored to specific Bootstrap versions or to provide alternate implementations that fix Shiny issues that are relevant to bslib but harder to address in Shiny directly.

To that last point, there are some deviations from core Shiny in this PR:

* `id` is used instead of `inputId` or `outputId`.
* `session` is not the first argument of the `update_*()` functions, instead it's the last.
* `...` are added in many places, generally following Shiny for Python's `*` placement. This matches practical usage and makes it easier for us to adjust function signatures in the future.
* We skip Shiny's icon validation in `input_action_button()` and `input_action_link()`, making it possible to use `bsicon::bs_icon()` and others.

Remaining work:

- [ ] modals
- [ ] notifications
- [ ] progress bars

